  "source_evidence": [
    "Asterinas pinned kernel/core/src/net/socket/unix/datagram/message.rs:195 propagates payload-copy failure before the ordinary pop_front at line 202.",
    "Linux reference net/core/datagram.c:183-202 unlinks ordinary receives; net/unix/af_unix.c:2558-2560,2598-2600 releases the selected datagram on copy failure. PEEK acquires a reference and retains the queue."
  ],
  "impact": "After ordinary EFAULT the same message and rights remain available to an Asterinas retry. This differs from Linux consumption, without itself being an unexplained reference leak."
